{"results":[{"url":"https://www.sixthandi.org/event/bryant-johnson/","final_url":"https://www.sixthandi.org/event/bryant-johnson/","title":"Bryant Johnson, Justice Ginsburg's Personal Trainer - Sixth & I","description":"The RBG Workout: How She Stays Strong . . . and You Can Too! walks you through how to do Justice Ginsburg’s workout—from planks to squats to (full) pushups—in the comfort of your home. Each exercise is demonstrated with full-color illustrations of the Justice in workout gear, always using perfect form, and also includes tips from the bench and sidebars with Johnson’s wisdom on getting fit and staying healthy.","language":"en","text":"## Talks & Entertainment\n\n### Event Details\n\nVenue:\n\nSixth & I\n\n## Bryant Johnson, Justice Ginsburg’s Personal Trainer\n\n### In Conversation with Isaac Dovere\n\n* This event has passed.\n\nHave you ever wondered what keeps Supreme Court Justice and octogenarian Ruth Bader Ginsburg so sprightly? She owes it in part to the twice-weekly workouts she does with her personal trainer, Bryant Johnson, someone she’s called “the most important person” in her life. Justice Ginsburg began training with Johnson in 1999, at the urging of her late husband, after she was treated for colon cancer.\n\nThe RBG Workout: How She Stays Strong . . . and You Can Too! walks you through how to do Justice Ginsburg’s workout—from planks to squats to (full) pushups—in the comfort of your home. Each exercise is demonstrated with full-color illustrations of the Justice in workout gear and also includes tips from the bench and sidebars with Johnson’s wisdom on getting fit and staying healthy. Johnson presents the workout exactly as he does it with Justice Ginsburg, along with some variations to accommodate skill level, personal preferences, and the equipment available.\n\nJohnson counts among his clients numerous Federal Court justices, judges, attorneys, and clerks. In addition to his day job as a court clerk, Johnson has been a member of the U.S. Army for over thirty years, twelve of those as a member of a Special Forces Airborne Unit.\n\nIn conversation with Isaac Dovere, Chief Washington Correspondent for Politico and the host of the Off Message podcast. Book signing to follow.\n\n* ##### Nov 9, 2026 • 7:00 pm ET\n\n  Rick Steves\n* ##### Nov 11, 2026 • 7:00 pm ET\n\n  LeVar Burton\n\n  In Conversation with Michele Norris\n* ##### Nov 12, 2026 • 7:00 pm ET\n\n  Yung Pueblo\n\n  In Conversation with Alex Elle\n* ##### Nov 14, 2026 • 7:30 pm ET\n\n  Minsoo Sohn, piano\n* ##### Nov 16, 2026 • 7:00 pm ET\n\n  CANCELED: Susan Spungen: Talk & Tasting\n\n  In Conversation with Claudia Fleming\n* ##### Nov 17, 2026 • 7:30 pm ET\n\n  Aga Khan Master Musicians\n* ##### Nov 18, 2026 • 7:00 pm ET\n\n  The New Yorker’s “Political Scene Podcast” Live\n\n  With Susan B. Glasser, Jane Mayer, and Evan Osnos\n* ##### Dec 1, 2026 • 7:00 pm ET\n\n  Dorinda Medley\n* ##### Dec 6, 2026 • 6:00 pm ET\n\n  Rebekah Lowin: Talk & Workshop\n\n  In Conversation with Rabbi Jenna Shaw\n* ##### Dec 17, 2026 • 8:00 pm ET\n\n  Haley Heynderickx\n\n  With John Roseboro\n* ##### Jan 31, 2027 • 3:00 pm ET\n\n  Gary Gulman’s 7th Hour: An All-New Standup Show – Early Show\n* ##### Jan 31, 2027 • 7:00 pm ET\n\n  Gary Gulman’s 7th Hour: An All-New Standup Show – Late Show","author":null,"published_date":"2017-08-18T17:51:49+00:00","latency_ms":1433.6824860074557,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}